    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 17 tests, 0 failures, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment feature, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, following the app's existing Spring conventions:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Database schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what makes the column exist; I updated all four dialects for consistency.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` response schema, alongside the existing derived `displayName`/`initials` fields. MapStruct then maps it automatically by name into the response DTO.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 assigns the code once, at creation time, right before saving:\n   - **LAST3** = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n   - **NNNN** = `String.format(\"%04d\", ...)` of `findAllOwners().size() + 1` \u2014 one more than the current number of owners, computed inside the same transaction so consecutively created owners get consecutive sequence numbers.\n\nThe Cp09 acceptance test verifies both the format (`SMI-`, `JON-` prefixes) and the global sequential numbering (second owner = first + 1), and it passes along with all pre-existing tests.",
